= February 2025 — A national rule or uneven local access

<span class="party-ko"><b>Barbara Nowacka</b></span>, KO politician and leader of Inicjatywa Polska, has become
the public face of two changes that opponents deliberately fold into one
culture war. Religion is reduced to one weekly lesson. A new health course—
mental health, prevention and sexual health included—must either reach every
pupil or depend on a parental opt-out.

Teachers need training, pupils need predictable access, parents want a voice,
and the Catholic hierarchy opposes the religion rule regardless of what
happens to health education. PSL can preserve the coalition by making the new
course optional; Lewica must decide whether that is a workable first year or a
map of the towns where knowledge will disappear. [? if not left_in_government:
We sit outside cabinet. We can organise teachers, table a bill and prove a
pilot, but we cannot issue the ministry's national rule.?]

- @schools_compulsory
- @schools_optional
- @schools_local
- @pis_school_bill
- @pis_school_coalition

@schools_compulsory
title: Insist on compulsory evidence-based health education
subtitle: Guarantee every pupil the same course and risk a revolt from PSL and church-backed parents.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: progressive_credibility += 5; young_support += 4; psl_relation -= 9; president_relation -= 4; government_coalition_dissent += 7; far_right_agenda += 4; public_mood_pending_secular_state_support += 11; public_mood_pending_secular_state_backlash += 7; public_mood_pending_secular_state_left_ownership += 8; public_mood_pending_secular_state_support += 8 if public_climate_progressive_index >= 48; public_mood_pending_secular_state_support -= 6 if public_climate_progressive_index < 48; news_headline = "The Left refuses an opt-out from public-health knowledge"

The ministry keeps health education in the common timetable and gives every
pupil the same entitlement. Teachers and medical educators gain a national
course to prepare for; PSL deputies and church-backed parent groups begin a
campaign to make the cabinet retreat before September.

- @poland_event_queue: File the compulsory curriculum

@schools_optional
title: Accept the opt-out and defend reducing religion to one lesson
subtitle: Keep an administrable reform alive, while accepting that access will depend on parents and place.
view-if: left_in_government = 1
on-arrival: government_delivery += 2; psl_relation += 3; progressives_dissent += 4; feminist_trust -= 2; public_trust += 1; public_mood_pending_secular_state_support += 3; public_mood_pending_secular_state_backlash += -3; news_headline = "The coalition narrows school reform to what it can administer"

Religion falls to one lesson, but health education opens with an opt-out. The
coalition can administer the compromise and Nowacka can train willing schools;
sexual-health and youth advocates know access will now depend most on the
parents and municipalities already least comfortable with the course.

- @poland_event_queue: File the optional settlement

@schools_local
title: Fund teachers and local pilots before another national fight
subtitle: Government: 1 budget capacity. Opposition: 1 resource for teacher training outside the ministry.
