= February 2025 — An opposition programme, not a ministerial decree

Prime Minister **[+ prime_minister +]** still heads a PiS cabinet, so the
historical ministry reform never becomes a national rule. <span class="party-ko"><b>Barbara Nowacka</b></span>
can supply an opposition draft. [? if left_in_government: Lewica serves inside
the cabinet, but PiS retains the education ministry; our ministers can force a
coalition argument, not issue its national rule.?][? if not
left_in_government: Lewica can supply organisers and a Sejm bill, but it does
not control the education ministry.?]

Teachers willing to run health classes, medical associations that can defend
the curriculum and parents who want their children included need a structure
that can outlast one press conference. We can prove the course locally, force
a defeated bill onto the record or build the coalition before asking it to
survive a PiS majority.

- @pis_school_pilots
- @pis_school_bill
- @pis_school_coalition

@pis_school_pilots
title: Coordinate municipal pilots and teacher training
subtitle: Cost: 1 resource. Proves the course locally without pretending to control the ministry.
choose-if: resources >= 1
unavailable-subtitle: The local programme has no organiser budget.
on-arrival: resources -= 1; local_network += 5; health_policy_pressure += 1; public_trust += 2; last_policy_stage = "Proposal"; last_policy_authority = "Opposition councils and teacher networks"; last_policy_implementation = 0; news_headline = "Opposition councils test health education without claiming national authority"

Lewica councillors recruit schools, teachers and local clinics for a common
pilot. Families in participating municipalities gain a real course and the
Sejm caucus gains evidence. The education minister remains free to ignore both;
no local success is presented as national implementation.

- @poland_event_queue: File the municipal pilot

